-## 4. Insights & Plan for Phase 3: Factories (`spec/fabricators/`)
-
-Profiling with `FPROF=1` shows that wasteful `after_create` hooks and default associations in `spec/fabricators/` still account for a large share of remaining factory execution time across both `spec/models` and `spec/requests`:
-
-1. **`spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb:11-13`**:
-   ```ruby
-   after_create do |status|
-     Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status)
-   end
-   ```
-   - Every `Fabricate(:status)` unconditionally creates a `Bookmark`, which in turn fabricates a new `Account`, `User`, and 2 `LoginActivity` records!
-   - In `spec/requests`, 304 out of 313 bookmarks (and in `spec/models`, 1,002 out of 1,019 bookmarks) were created solely by this `after_create` hook on `:status` and never used. Removing this hook will cut `Fabricate(:status)` time in half.
-
-2. **`spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb:16-18`**:
-   ```ruby
-   after_create do |user|
-     2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) }
-   end
-   ```
-   - Every `Fabricate(:user)` unconditionally creates 2 `LoginActivity` records (756 unused `LoginActivity` inserts in `spec/requests` and 270 in `spec/models`). Removing this hook eliminates 2 `INSERT` queries per user.
-
-3. **`spec/fabricators/account_fabricator.rb:13`**:
-   ```ruby
-   user { |attrs| attrs[:domain].nil? ? Fabricate.build(:user, account: nil) : nil }
-   ```
-   - Every local `Account` fabricates a `User` (even though `Account` does not require a `User` in the database or model validations unless the spec tests `account.user`).
+## 4. Phase 3 Root Causes & Optimizations Applied: Factories (`spec/fabricators/`) & Factory Usage
+
+1. **Removed Wasteful `after_create` Hooks (`spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb`, `spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`)**:
+   - `status_fabricator.rb` previously ran `after_create { |status| Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status) }`, which unconditionally fabricated a new `Bookmark`, `Account`, `Keypair`, `User`, and 2 `LoginActivity` records (16 extra SQL queries!) on every `Fabricate(:status)` call. Removing this hook reduced `status` factory time by >50% and eliminated ~700 unused `Bookmark` creations across `spec/models` and `spec/requests`.
+   - `user_fabricator.rb` previously ran `after_create { |user| 2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) } }`, which inserted 2 unused `LoginActivity` rows on every `User` creation (~986 unused inserts across `spec/models` and `spec/requests`).
+
+2. **Eliminated Per-Account `Keypair` Row & OpenSSL Key Generation Overhead (`spec/fabricators/account_fabricator.rb`, `spec/fabricators/keypair_fabricator.rb`, `spec/fabricators/web_push_subscription_fabricator.rb`, `spec/fabricators/webauthn_credential_fabricator.rb`)**:
+   - Local accounts in `account_fabricator.rb` now set `public_key` and `private_key` directly (`SigningKeysHelpers::PUBLIC_RSA_TEST_KEY` / `PRIVATE_RSA_TEST_KEY`), avoiding 2 `Keypair` uniqueness `SELECT`s, 1 `INSERT INTO "keypairs"`, and AES-GCM `ActiveRecord::Encryption` of the 1,679-byte RSA private key on every local `Account` creation while preserving `account.keypair` behavior via `Keypair.from_legacy_account`.
+   - Changed `keypair_fabricator.rb` from `account { Fabricate(:account, keypairs: []) }` (which triggered `Account#generate_keys` -> `OpenSSL::PKey::RSA.new(2048)` taking ~40ms) to `account { Fabricate.build(:account) }`.
+   - Replaced per-call `OpenSSL::PKey::EC.generate('prime256v1')` in `web_push_subscription_fabricator.rb` and `webauthn_credential_fabricator.rb` with precomputed/memoized test keys.
+
+3. **Eliminated Duplicate / Optional Default Associations & Slow `Faker` Sequences in Fabricators**:
+   - Removed optional `reference_account` from `canonical_email_block_fabricator.rb` and optional `parent_account` from `conversation_fabricator.rb`.
+   - Deduplicated shared `account` / `status` associations in `poll_fabricator.rb`, `status_trend_fabricator.rb`, `status_pin_fabricator.rb`, `notification_request_fabricator.rb`, `custom_filter_status_fabricator.rb`, `media_attachment_fabricator.rb`, `account_conversation_fabricator.rb`, `report_note_fabricator.rb`, and `web_push_subscription_fabricator.rb` so that child associations reuse the parent's `account` instead of fabricating a second/third `Account` + `User`.
+   - Replaced slow `Faker::Internet.user_name` / `Faker::Internet.email` / `Faker::Internet.domain_name` / `Faker::Lorem.word` calls inside high-frequency sequence blocks (`account`, `user`, `tag`, `domain_block`, `email_domain_block`, `username_block`, `canonical_email_block`) with lightweight deterministic sequences (`"user_#{i}"`, `"user_#{i}@mastodon.test"`, etc.).
+
+4. **Optimized Factory Usage in `spec/models` and `spec/requests`**:
+   - Consolidated duplicated `let_it_be` / `let` factory setups and reused existing accounts/statuses in `spec/models` (`trends/statuses_spec.rb`, `public_feed_spec.rb`, `tag_feed_spec.rb`, `notification_spec.rb`, `status_spec.rb`, `account_spec.rb`, `report_spec.rb`, `media_attachment_spec.rb`, `status/visibility_spec.rb`, `fasp/backfill_request_spec.rb`, `relationship_filter_spec.rb`, `export_spec.rb`, `featured_tag_spec.rb`, `status_pin_spec.rb`, `admin/moderation_action_spec.rb`, `web/push_subscription_spec.rb`, `concerns/account/interactions_spec.rb`, `concerns/status/fasp_concern_spec.rb`, `account_suggestions/friends_of_friends_source_spec.rb`).
+   - Consolidated per-example factory calls into shared `let_it_be` / `before_all` setups in `spec/requests` (`api/v1/statuses_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/reports_spec.rb`, `api/v1/notifications_spec.rb`, `api/v2/notifications_spec.rb`, `api/v1/notifications/requests_spec.rb`, `api/v1/lists/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/collections_spec.rb`, `api/v1/collection_items_spec.rb`, `api/v1/follow_requests_spec.rb`, `api/v1/bookmarks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/favourites_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/bookmarks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/favourites_spec.rb`, `api/v2/search_spec.rb`, `api/web/embeds_spec.rb`, `api/v1/directories_spec.rb`, `api/v1/push/subscriptions_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/account_actions_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/canonical_email_blocks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts/follower_accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts/following_accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts/relationships_spec.rb`, `activitypub/followers_synchronizations_spec.rb`, `collection_items_spec.rb`, `self_destruct_spec.rb`, `admin/accounts_spec.rb`, `admin/collections_spec.rb`, `admin/reports_spec.rb`, `admin/roles_spec.rb`, `admin/username_blocks_spec.rb`).
+
+### `spec/models` Results After Phase 3
+- **Wall Time**: **~20.3 seconds** (down from **28.5 seconds** after Phase 1 / **27.9s** before Phase 3 — **28.8% faster in Phase 3**; down from **154.5 seconds** at baseline — **86.9% faster / 7.6x speedup**)
+- **SQL Queries (`sql.active_record`)**: **27,225 queries (3.29s)** (down from **43,757 queries / 5.02s** before Phase 3 and **113,959 queries / 20.90s** at baseline — **76.1% total reduction**)
+- **Factory Calls (`FPROF=1`)**: **1,808 total / 1,700 top-level (12.24s)** (down from **2,647 total / 21.01s** before Phase 3 and **4,721 total / 141.35s** at baseline — **91.3% total reduction in factory time**)
+- **Examples**: 1,795 examples, 0 failures
+
+### `spec/requests` Results After Phase 3
+- **Wall Time**: **~35.9 seconds** (down from **46.0 seconds** after Phase 2 — **22.0% faster in Phase 3**; down from **140.6 seconds** before Phase 2 / **~180s+** at baseline — **74.5%+ faster / 3.9x–5.0x speedup**)
+- **SQL Queries (`sql.active_record`)**: **49,731 queries (4.93s)** (down from **77,308 queries / 7.99s** after Phase 2 and **236,860 queries / 23.00s** before Phase 2 — **79.0% total reduction**)
+- **Factory Calls (`FPROF=1`)**: **1,720 total / 1,688 top-level (8.90s)** (down from **3,192 total / 16.86s** after Phase 2 and **11,030 total / 91.81s** before Phase 2 — **90.3% total reduction in factory time**)
+- **Examples**: 1,877 examples, 0 failures
+
+### Combined `spec/models` + `spec/requests` Progress
+- **Baseline Combined Wall Time**: ~295.1 seconds (~4 minutes 55 seconds; >330s before Phase 1 global fixes)
+- **After Phase 2 Combined Wall Time**: ~74.8 seconds (`spec/models`: ~28.5s + `spec/requests`: ~46.3s)
+- **After Phase 3 Combined Wall Time**: **~56.2 seconds** (`spec/models`: ~20.3s + `spec/requests`: ~35.9s — **24.9% faster in Phase 3**, and **81.0% faster / 5.25x speedup overall**)
+
+---
+
+## 5. Insights & Notes for Future Optimization Runs
+
+- Other spec directories (`spec/controllers`, `spec/services`, `spec/workers`, `spec/serializers`, `spec/lib`, `spec/views`, `spec/presenters`, `spec/policies`, `spec/helpers`, `spec/validators`, `spec/mailers`) automatically benefit from the `spec/fabricators/` optimizations above (removal of `Bookmark` and `LoginActivity` `after_create` hooks, local `Account` legacy keypair fast-path, deduplicated associations, and faster sequences).
+- If optimizing `spec/controllers`, `spec/services`, or `spec/workers` in future phases:
+  - Consider extending `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` and `PaperclipTestOptimization` defaults to `type: :controller`, `type: :service`, and `type: :worker` (with `:inline_workers` / `:paperclip_processing` opt-in tags).
+  - Use `let_it_be` and `before_all` for shared read-only setups in large controller and service specs.
+  - Note: When using nested `before_all` blocks that mutate associations (like `account.follow!`) on outer `let_it_be` records that may have been mutated in earlier sibling examples, call `.reload` on those `let_it_be` records at the start of `before_all` because `let_it_be`'s automatic `:reload` modifier runs in `before(:each)`, which executes after `before_all`.
